## Finding a student

Two routes:

- **My Class → Students** — your own roster, which is where you will usually start.
- **Students → Student Search** — everyone, if you have been granted it. Search by name or Student
  ID; ID is faster and unambiguous where names repeat.

Selecting a student opens their profile.

## What's on the profile

The student's details, and then their history: attendance over the month and the term, exam results
across subjects, and payments where you can see them.

The most useful thing here for a teacher is the combination. A drop in results that lines up with a
drop in attendance is a different conversation from one that doesn't, and the profile is the one
place both are on the same screen.

## Reading the attendance figures honestly

The monthly and term attendance on a profile are built from the same records you create each
morning. A student who looks like they have missed a fortnight may simply have been in a class where
the register wasn't completed. Before raising it with a family, check the class's own attendance for
those dates — see
[Read Your Class's Attendance](/docs/educonnect-teacher-class-attendance).

## What you can and can't change

You can read a profile. Editing student records, moving a student between classes, and deleting
anyone are office actions — and Student ID and Class cannot be edited at all once a student exists,
by anyone. See [Add a Student](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student).

